WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:05.590
Stranger Things season 3 is an official Internet-breaker,
but recently, the beloved series garnered

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:10.360
attention for all the wrong reasons: It turns
out the new season includes a little production

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.620
error that slipped right past most viewers.

00:00:13.129 --> 00:00:16.920
As far as spoilers are concerned, we won't
be getting into anything major here, but we

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.380
will be touching upon some general story points.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:20.840
Consider yourself warned!

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:26.180
Hawk-eyed fans of the show spotted a continuity
error during the fifth episode of season three,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.820
which hit Netflix on July 4th.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:32.800
The episode, entitled "Chapter Five: The Flayed,"
finds the gang loitering around the local

00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:37.730
hospital, where Nancy is visiting Doris Driscoll,
a woman linked to the season's big supernatural

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:38.220
threat.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:42.380
While Nancy gets herself into a spot of trouble,
the rest of the gang hangs out in the waiting

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:42.880
room.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:47.659
That's when Eleven uses her powers to short-circuit
the hospital vending machine to give Mike

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:49.580
and Lucas lots of snacks to share.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.700
Because that's just what good friends do.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:02.700
Trying to win back Eleven after acting like
a jerk, Mike gives her a few M&amp;M's as a peace

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:03.200
offering.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.960
But look closely at that handful of chocolate
candies.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.420
Do you see what we see?

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:08.960
There's a red M&amp;M.

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.320
This season of Stranger Things is set in 1985,
a time when red M&amp;M's were impossible to find.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:20.160
People born in the era of plentiful red M&amp;M's
probably didn't think twice about this tiny

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:20.920
little detail.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:25.640
But the fact is, Mars Inc., the makers of
the candy-shell-coated chocolates, actually

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:29.410
discontinued that particular color of M&amp;M
back in the 1970s.

00:01:29.410 --> 00:01:33.060
And they didn't bring back red M&amp;M's until
1987.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:38.480
The company discontinued that particular color
because of the so-called "red dye scare" of

00:01:38.480 --> 00:01:38.980
1976.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.420
That's when the Food and Drug Administration
published a study linking common food additives

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:49.220
Red Dye #2 and Red Dye #4 to cancer, ruling
that red dyes weren't safe for consumption.

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:54.130
Though Mars used a different red food dye
to make its red M&amp;M's, the company nonetheless

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:58.280
replaced red M&amp;Ms with orange shortly after
the FDA made its ruling.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:01.760
The company hoped this would calm people down
and keep business booming.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.980
Eleven years later, red M&amp;M's came back and
never left.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:10.360
So unless Mike has his own very special power,
there's absolutely no way he could have given

00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:15.730
Eleven a red M&amp;M in 1985, unless the vending
machine at Hawkins Memorial Hospital hadn't

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:17.520
been restocked in almost a decade.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.380
"Boy I really hope someone got fired for that blunder."

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.060
Of course, anything is possible in that town.

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.650
At the end of the day, this goof isn't half
as bad as Game of Thrones' infamous coffee

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.080
cup gaffe during its eighth and final season.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:38.940
That incident involved a paper coffee cup
ending up on set, widely believed to be from

00:02:38.940 --> 00:02:43.160
Starbucks, but actually from a local café
in Northern Ireland where the series was filmed.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.150
The now-notorious cup ended up making it into
the episode's final cut, and no one involved

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.620
with the show noticed…until it was too late.

00:02:51.340 --> 00:02:55.200
Compared to that mistake, the blip in Stranger
Things is small potatoes.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:03:00.120
And even though Netflix and the Stranger Things
team have yet to address the error, the official

00:03:00.120 --> 00:03:02.950
M&amp;M's Twitter account offered up its own explanation:

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:07.680
"Clearly, in 1985 Red M&amp;M's were around...in
the Upside Down."

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.180
Well-played, M&amp;M's.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:11.060
What a delicious little joke.

